 **Sprint summary.** Seven tissue and plasma validations (VAL-058 through VAL-064) all PASS at the prereg-sealed Cohen's d ≥ 0.5 threshold, plus one exploratory urine-arm specimen comparison (VAL-065), plus the pancreatic-epic v0.1 build (VAL-066/067/068/069) which delivered three independent tissue cohorts plus a directional Xu-538 fallback panel. Two framework-relevant stratification findings emerged: (1) **smoking stratification is mandatory for lung-epic** — TCGA-LUAD is 76% ever-smoker and the never-smoker arm (n=2) is underpowered for independent inference. (2) **Chronic viral hepatitis blunts the paired tumor-vs-adjacent-normal contrast in HCC** through methylation drift in the adjacent-normal liver tissue ("field defect" per Villanueva 2015), shrinking the paired contrast even though the tumor architecture is genuinely disrupted. Non-viral HCC (alcohol/NAFLD) shows classical secretory-class magnitude (d ≈ +0.66, comparable to breast secretory). The pattern parallels the lung smoking finding and may generalize: chronic disease-driver exposures drive adjacent-normal field defects that need to be controlled for in paired-tissue analyses. **VAL-065 is exploratory:** GSE119260 (Brikun 2018) is the only public EPIC 850K urine methylation prostate cohort and contains only n=4 advanced-disease patients (all bone metastatic, Gleason 4+4 to 5+5). Sample size precludes substrate-vs-substrate inference. The observed urine vs benign tissue paired d = −2.39 (urine A-score dramatically lower than benign tissue in all 4 patients) was anticipated by the pre-registration as O5_UNEXPECTED and is documented as an open question pending a larger urine methylation prostate cohort with healthy controls and mixed disease stages.
 
@@ -162,6 +164,8 @@ A second sprint of validations testing per-cancer architectural disruption signa
 
 **Heme-epic build (VAL-082).** First per-patient validation of the heme-epic myeloid arm at the blood-level methylation that v1 EDEAR will actually run. **VAL-082 GSE62298 Glass 2017 AML HM450 (n=68) vs GSE51057 EPIC-Italy menarche cohort cancer-free buffy coat healthy controls (n=115 QC) produced ΔA = +0.1039 above Italian healthy baseline; Cohen's d = +3.71 [+3.23, +4.20] p ≈ 0; 98.5% of AML samples scoring above the Italian healthy 95th percentile, 91.2% above the 99th percentile.** This is the strongest single-cohort effect size measured anywhere in the Cookbook to date. The structural reason: AML is a myeloid-lineage cancer where the cancer cells ARE neutrophil/monocyte progenitors, and the Xu-538 panel was trained on whole-blood buffy coat where ~50-75% of cells are neutrophils. AML in blood is the case where the universal Stage 1 panel reads the disease cells directly rather than reading a small contaminant fraction against an immune-cell background. Hematologic cancers are the natural strength of cfDNA/buffy-coat methylation screening. VAL-082 also resets framework number expectations: Issue 002's prediction of A_AML ≈ 1.10 with ΔA = +0.168 is a **5-substrate combined cfDNA prediction** (future L2/L3 platform target), NOT directly comparable to v1 single-substrate methyl-only buffy-coat scoring. At v1, AML reads at A = 0.54 against Italian healthy 0.44 with d = +3.71 — this is the v1-deployment effect size and is sufficient for clinical-grade detection. The lymphoid arms (B-cell CLL/DLBCL/MM, T-cell thymoma) cannot reach single_cohort_validated tier from publicly-accessible 450K data alone — the long-window pre-diagnostic CLL data exists (EnviroGenomarkers Florence-Umeå 2.0-15.7 yr pre-dx; MCCS up to 18 yr pre-dx) but sits at biobank-gated access tier requiring formal applications, the same access pattern as VAL-046 Rotterdam pre-dx pancreatic and Bukowski CINCS pre-dx cervical. heme-epic v0.1 ships with myeloid arm at single_cohort_validated tier and lymphoid arms at framework_calibrated_pending_per_patient_validation tier. **Brain-cancer differential gap documented**: Moss 2018 reference does not include brain/CNS, so "Moss NULL on solid organs" does not exclude CNS disease — glioma-epic (TBD) will handle the CNS pathway separately, and v1 patient reports must surface "uniform Stage 3 elevation + Moss NULL on peripherals" as a pattern that warrants neurological evaluation alongside other differentials.
 
+**Glioma-epic build (VAL-088 + VAL-089).** Two specimen pathways tested in the v0.1 build of the structurally-hardest card in the cookbook. Glioma-epic's primary detection class is **terminal** (neurons, oligodendrocytes, astrocytes; H_min = 0.7728), which contributes only ~0.5% of plasma cfDNA at healthy baseline — below the Moss 4% detection floor. Single-timepoint plasma deconvolution returns null even when brain pathology is present. The card is built as a **multi-pathway reference document** with five detection pathways documented: cfMeDIP-seq plasma (Pathway 1, different chemistry from v1 array deployment), deep cervical lymph node aspirate via meningeal lymphatic drainage (Pathway 2, no published cohort), multi-specimen tier system from LP-CSF gold-standard down to whole blood (Pathway 3), brain-resident immune trafficking signature (Pathway 4, directional panel pending construction), and direction-as-discriminator (Pathway 5, REVISED by VAL-088). Three findings emerged: (1) **CCL-023 cell-fraction prior was inverted by direct measurement.** Bracci 2022's published cell-fraction signature (lymphocytes-down, neutrophils-up, an NLR-style shift) had been used as the literature anchor predicting NEGATIVE A-score direction for glioma. VAL-088 measured POSITIVE direction d = +0.91. **Cell-fraction direction (NLR-style) and methylation-entropy direction (A-score Shannon entropy) are different metrics measuring different phenomena.** Glioma joins the activation-shifted set (AD, breast, lung, prostate, HCC), not the suppression-shifted set (CRC). Revised CCL-023 anchoring set: pre-diagnostic CRC at 5-10yr window reads NEGATIVE; everything else (AD, breast, lung, prostate, HCC, pancreatic, glioma) at-diagnosis or post-diagnosis reads POSITIVE. Direction-as-discriminator may collapse to "early-pre-dx CRC is the outlier." (2) **Shannon entropy of methylation captures cell-mixture diversity, NOT tumor-cell intrinsic property.** VAL-089 cultured glioma spheres (n=4) scored d = -1.81 NEGATIVE direction vs non-tumor brain controls — pure tumor-cell-line β distributions are LESS architecturally entropic than mixed-cell tissue containing neurons + glia + microglia + endothelium + neoplastic cells. **A high A-score is a heterogeneity marker, not a tumor marker.** Tumor TISSUE produces high A-score because tumor tissue contains many cell types in mixture, not because tumor CELLS have intrinsically high entropy. This is a fundamental biology cross-check for the framework with applicability beyond glioma — cell-line vs primary-tissue comparisons will systematically differ in A-score, and tumor purity adjustment matters for tissue-pathway interpretation. (3) **The card IS the multi-pathway reference document.** Per glioma-LL-003 the v0.1 README includes a TL;DR routing table, per-pathway "what we can do today / what we'd need" sections, multi-specimen tier table, commercial.web.py decision tree with seven routing arms, patient-report templates per arm including the "no immediate culprit found" 10-year-out scenario, and a priority-ordered "what we'd need access to" explicit asks list (top priority: dbGaP phs001497.v2.p1 UCSF AGS Bracci 2022 with 139 pre-surgery glioma + 454 on-study controls). Honest weaknesses summary explicitly enumerated: single-cohort blood-arm validation; no pre-diagnostic data; no CSF data validated; no cfMeDIP-seq integration; CCL-023 prior inverted; no discrimination from AD on Stage 1 direction alone (both read positive — Stage 2 + Stage 3 + clinical context required for differential). glioma-epic v0.1 ships with blood arm at `exploratory_pending_replication` tier and tissue arm at `single_cohort_validated_with_substrate_scope_caveat` tier; CSF / cfMeDIP-seq plasma / lymphatic arms at `pre-validation_skeleton` tier with explicit upgrade paths documented.
+
 ### Healthy baseline reference tables (8 classes × 10 age decades, 80 cells) — April 18, 2026
 
 Companion to the cascade: per-age-decade expected healthy A-score for every architecture class. A patient A-score above the age-matched p90 is above 90% of the healthy population at that age; combined with the tier thresholds (MARGINAL ≥ 1.01, DETECTABLE ≥ 1.05, URGENT ≥ 1.07, FLOOR BREACH ≥ 1.10), this provides a two-axis clinical readout (age-percentile × tier).
